1
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:42,240
onto the head of the
carpenter who'd been saving up.

4
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:48,440
They laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:55,660
Even if you stir up some spirit,
Katsushika Kameari.

6
00:00:55,660 --> 00:01:02,540
Even a yawn changes nothing,
and the streets feel strangely gentle.

7
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:14,660
From the pointed-hat water
tower up to the vast sky,

8
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,800
the sun goes down.

9
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:25,280
Why does tomorrow end too

10
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:30,280
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness is lost again.

11
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:33,860
Because I'm a fool who
only just realized it.

12
00:01:58,540 --> 00:01:59,980
Morning, Ryo-chan.

13
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,480
Reiko, good morning.

14
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:04,040
Here's your tea.

15
00:02:04,660 --> 00:02:06,600
Don't you have any snacks
or something to go with it?

16
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:09,260
You ate them all the day before yesterday,
Ryo-chan.

17
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:11,300
You should've bought more.

18
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:14,880
If I buy more now,
they'll just end up as your meal.

19
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:23,500
Ugh, now I'm even hungrier.

20
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:26,560
Payday is still three whole days away.

21
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:29,840
At this rate, I'm going to starve to death.

22
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:34,840
Reiko, please, just 1,000 yen.
Just 1,000 yen is all I need.

23
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:38,340
No way. I've been told not to lend you a single yen,
Ryo-chan.

24
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:40,820
Chief Ohara gave me strict orders.

25
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:43,280
Yeah, that demon of a chief.

26
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:47,680
There you are.

27
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:50,240
Welcome, Mr. Honda.

28
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,140
Oh my?

29
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,060
What happened to your face?

30
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,100
It's nothing serious.

31
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:01,520
Actually, it's a big deal, senpai.

32
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:03,520
What on earth is it, then?

33
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,540
A father-son fight?

34
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,860
So you want me to mediate that?

35
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:15,460
My father and my younger brother Fumitaka
have been fighting nonstop lately.

36
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:18,940
My sister asked me to go mediate, but

37
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:20,520
this is what happened to me.

38
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:24,160
Please, senpai, you have to do something!

39
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:29,520
I'm broke until payday and have no time
to worry about other people's problems.

40
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:34,100
Come on, senpai,
you're the only one I can rely on.

41
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:37,780
Besides,
I haven't had a decent meal in a week.

42
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:39,900
I don't have the energy to mediate.

43
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:43,613
My sister Il is great at cooking.

44
00:03:43,663 --> 00:03:46,500
I'll have her prepare plenty
of your favorite dishes.

45
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:47,640
Really?

46
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:53,200
So, what's the cause of the fight?

47
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,340
Apparently they're arguing over whether
he should take over his father's shop.

48
00:03:57,560 --> 00:04:00,620
Your family runs a motorcycle shop, right?

49
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:05,460
Yeah, that's why I was riding
motorcycles before I could even remember.

50
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:12,600
Yeah, you're a hardcore motorcycle rider.

51
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:14,380
Move aside, move aside! If we die, we die!

52
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,280
We're here, this is it.

53
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:25,420
Is it closed today?

54
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:27,300
No, that's strange.

55
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:31,120
Dad isn't the type to take
a day off for just anything.

56
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:37,120
Did he close up because
he heard senpai was coming?

57
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:40,820
Right, then please take
care of things, senpai.

58
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,020
I'm home.

59
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,380
Welcome back, big brother.

60
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:48,760
So you're Ibu-chan.

61
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,500
Hey, hey, hey, what's going on?

62
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:56,400
No, senpai, you can't just
suddenly talk to her like that.

63
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:59,100
My little sister is really
shy around strangers.

64
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:01,000
Don't overdo it.

65
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:03,500
There, there, come on out.

66
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:06,000
This is Mr. Ryotsu,
the one you talked to on the phone.

67
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,980
Hey, but he's not a bad guy, okay?

68
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:11,620
Come on, it's fine, really.

69
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:15,900
Like a dog or a cat

70
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:18,340
Well then, let me introduce everyone.

71
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:22,140
My dad and my younger brother, Fumitaka.

72
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:23,960
But everyone calls him Monkey.

73
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:26,360
This is my senior, Ryotsu-san.

74
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:30,040
Thank you always for looking after Hayato.

75
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:31,960
I'm Kaizo, Hayato's father.

76
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:32,960
I'm Fumitaka.

77
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:34,660
Nice to meet you.

78
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:42,440
Nice to meet you. Why is the shop closed today, Dad?
Were you cleaning up, Monkey?

79
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:49,680
Wait, didn't the two of them have a fight?
No way, it must be some kind of mistake.

80
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:56,600
They're getting along just fine!
Yes, we can eat without any trouble!

81
00:05:58,820 --> 00:06:02,940
How beautiful it is when family gets along.
Fighting is not allowed.

82
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:29,940
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

83
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:38,960
I've eaten, I've eaten! It's been a week
since I had a proper meal, hasn't it?

84
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:40,920
Is that so?

85
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:45,100
Hey, Ibu, bring the umeboshi.
Let's make ochazuke.

86
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:49,940
Ochazuke? That sounds great! Itadakimasu.

87
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:59,600
Mr. Ryotsu,
are you interested in motorcycles?

88
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:02,740
I love anything that has the word
"mechanical" attached to it.

89
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:06,620
Especially motorcycles. I always ride with Honda,
so I've become oddly knowledgeable about them.

90
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:09,220
Well then, why don't you take
a look at our motorcycles too?

91
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:14,040
What is this?

92
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:16,800
Isn't that a Rikuo motorcycle?

93
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:18,560
Why is something like this here?

94
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:22,360
Honda, was your family's business
a used motorcycle dealership?

95
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,920
No, we only sell new bikes.

96
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:27,700
Then what's this Rikuo doing here?

97
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:30,920
It's a motorcycle from a company that went bankrupt decades ago,
you know.

98
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,140
Well, if we're talking about that,

99
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:34,140
we also have a new Meguro, though.

100
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:37,820
That's also a company from long ago,
isn't it?

101
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:41,800
The recent ones are things like
the Mach 3 and the Double One,

102
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:45,140
but they're all bikes
from over twenty years ago!

103
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:48,300
They just haven't been selling very well.

104
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:49,680
Not selling?

105
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,500
So what are you selling them for, anyway?

106
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,260
They're all at list price.

107
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:56,240
List price, as in the price
when they were first released?

108
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:58,340
Well, they're vehicles, after all.

109
00:07:58,920 --> 00:07:59,820
Eeeeeeh?!

110
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:00,640
2

111
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:05,820
These are the kind of bikes that would
make any motorcycle enthusiast drool.

112
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:09,400
They could sell for four, five,
even ten times the American price.

113
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:12,880
Father?

114
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:16,060
Could you possibly sell me this bike too?

115
00:08:16,060 --> 00:08:17,780
Yone-senpai's fine, I guess.

116
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:21,660
I've become completely captivated by the appeal of motorcycles,
you see.

117
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:25,240
Let's go touring together sometime,
shall we?

118
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:26,900
Do you think so, Honda-kun?

119
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:29,320
N-no way, senpai...

120
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,560
Sell it to someone else and make a killing.

121
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:34,360
I just want to ride motorcycles,
purely for the love of it.

122
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:37,680
Don't say such stupid things, Honda-kun.

123
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:40,660
Since it's a favor from Hayato's senpai,
after all.

124
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:42,980
Alright, which one will it be?

125
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:47,380
Don't buy several at once.
It'd look suspicious.

126
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:49,300
If we're narrowing it down to just one...

127
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:51,480
It's the Rikuo, of course.

128
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:53,540
It's a classic from
nearly half a century ago.

129
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:58,000
It should be trading at several times that,
over 2 million yen.

130
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:01,700
And in condition this good,
it'd fetch 3 million yen.

131
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:04,140
After all, it's unused and brand new.

132
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:07,880
Excuse me, could I have this Rikuo?

133
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,500
A Rikuo, you say?

134
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:14,620
Damn, I should've gone
for a Meguro Junior instead.

135
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:15,980
Sure thing.

136
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:16,660
Oh my.

137
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:21,680
Well, there's some paperwork to take care of,
so please wait a moment.

138
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:24,380
Honda's old man seems like a pretty decent guy,
doesn't he?

139
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:27,180
It's strange that none of
these are selling at all.

140
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,200
Senpai, are you really going to buy it?

141
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:31,920
Of course,
all that's left is the paperwork, right?

142
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:33,820
That paperwork is a real pain, you know.

143
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:42,440
What?

144
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:54,240
Fifty years devoted to motorcycles.

145
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:57,540
I'm the motorcycle demon of Senju.

146
00:09:57,540 --> 00:09:59,640
W-wait, your father?

147
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:02,900
Yes, once he puts on his overalls,
his personality changes.

148
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:05,380
Just like Honda's father.

149
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:09,700
Ryotsu, you said you wanted a Rikuo,
didn't you?

150
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:11,760
Uh, well, sort of.

151
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:16,880
"Sort of"?! You think you can lay a finger
on our Rikuo with that half-hearted attitude?!

152
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:19,260
Eh I'm serious, sir!

153
00:10:19,260 --> 00:10:21,136
I've been smitten with
this bike for ten years,

154
00:10:21,186 --> 00:10:24,140
and I've been wishing with
all my heart to get it.

155
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:32,620
You want it that badly? Then yes,
you'll take the Rikuo-class test. Test.

156
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:33,880
me

157
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:53,320
What the hell! Why is there a test course behind the house? Are you testing every single customer?
No, not every one.

158
00:10:56,240 --> 00:11:00,020
Anyone who isn't qualified to take
the test gets turned away on the spot.

159
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:02,600
Then you won't sell much of anything,
will you.

160
00:11:03,340 --> 00:11:06,760
For the Rikuo,
you'll have to take a ten-stage test.

161
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:10,700
Then, first up is the first test:
the love test.

162
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:15,640
When I went touring, I found an old
motorcycle abandoned at the bottom of a valley.

163
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,020
What would you do?

164
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:20,260
What do you mean, what would I do?
There's nothing you can do about that.

165
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:21,060
Idiot!

166
00:11:21,060 --> 00:11:24,460
A true motorcycle lover would
at least try hauling it up.

167
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:30,220
Make it work, even if it's hard! If you can't,
you should at least give it a proper funeral!

168
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:33,200
Y-yes, sir!
Of course, that's exactly what I meant!

169
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:38,240
Good! Now carry this bike up that cliff!

170
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:46,780
I'd like to ask one thing...

171
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:47,380
What?

172
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:50,240
Why are there so many weights attached?

173
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:56,720
What if you found a Rikuo Star
Q7-type Hayaguruma lying around?

174
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,980
The weight is 500 kilos, you know!

175
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:03,800
500 kilos isn't something a human can lift!

176
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:07,180
That's where your love for
motorcycles comes in to cover it.

177
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:09,500
That's why it's a test of love.

178
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:11,820
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

179
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:14,740
This is also so you can get a Rikuo Star.

180
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:18,340
Yay!

181
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:23,980
Good! You've cleared the first test!
Next up, the second test!

182
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:30,855
On a touring ride, I found an old
motorcycle abandoned in a river.

183
00:12:30,905 --> 00:12:32,140
What would you do?

184
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:35,120
It's probably rusted and useless, but...

185
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:37,660
You wouldn't just leave it there,
would you...

186
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:39,480
Of course I'll go get it!

187
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,760
All for the sake of getting the Rikuo,
I suppose...

188
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:46,400
Whoa! What the--! It suddenly got deep!

189
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:49,660
Natural rivers can hide
all sorts of dangers!

190
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:50,980
Doesn't even hurt...

191
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:55,820
Someone might have
released piranhas in there.

192
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:57,600
As if that'd happen!

193
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:02,580
Good, next, the third test.

194
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:10,680
On a touring ride, I found an old
motorcycle abandoned high up in a tree.

195
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:12,180
What would you do?

196
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:15,720
Of course I'll go get it.

197
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:19,340
It's all for the Rikuo, after all.

198
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:33,260
Test five.

199
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:36,620
When you went touring, your motorcycle

200
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:39,440
was taken apart into pieces by some
good-for-nothing in the mountains.

201
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:40,940
What would you do?

202
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,020
Just put it back together, right?

203
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:47,900
Aaaaah! Alright, on to test six!

204
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:52,140
Test seven. Test eight.

205
00:13:52,620 --> 00:14:01,080
Test nine is written. Let's see, name the origin
of the name of the prewar motorcycle maker Cabton.

206
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:05,820
Wasn't it
"Come and buy two," Nakagawa of Osaka?

207
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,580
Is it done?

208
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:14,200
A score of 62, just barely, but you pass.

209
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:15,940
Knowledge test cleared!

210
00:14:15,940 --> 00:14:17,920
Next is the final test.

211
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:18,660
Yes!

212
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:20,420
The final test is...

213
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:21,700
that one.

214
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:27,780
Wait, you don't mean I have
to go through that, do you?

215
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:29,580
This isn't a circus, you know!

216
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:34,000
If you wandered into an old hula
hoop factory while out touring,

217
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,380
and the factory caught fire,

218
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:37,640
what would you do?

219
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:40,160
Well, it's fine if I just go for it, right?

220
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,520
After coming this far,
I'm not giving up now!

221
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:43,640
Time out!

222
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:48,140
Here, a monkey wrench.

223
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:49,660
What is it, Ito-san?

224
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:51,560
If you have time to go out gallivanting,

225
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:54,620
why don't you study up
on motorcycles a little?

226
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:56,660
Even if you say that to me,

227
00:14:56,660 --> 00:15:00,700
how can I become a proper motorcycle
shop owner riding a bicycle?

228
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:03,140
But I'm still in junior high school.

229
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:07,240
Hey, didn't you two already
settle your father-son fight?

230
00:15:08,580 --> 00:15:11,140
Earlier I held back since
there were customers around,

231
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:15,440
but it won't be settled until this
kid says he'll take over the shop.

232
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:18,380
If you keep saying that,
if you keep saying that,

233
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:20,600
you'll end up riding a bicycle, you know.

234
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:23,920
What are you going to do, riding a bicycle?

235
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:27,880
N-no way...

236
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:30,460
Fourteen years devoted solely to bicycles.

237
00:15:30,460 --> 00:15:32,740
Honda family's second son, Monkey Honda.

238
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:36,540
I'll turn this shop into a
bicycle store in my generation.

239
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:37,164
Hah...

240
00:15:37,214 --> 00:15:41,260
My younger brother's personality
changes when he rides a bicycle.

241
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:43,660
Typical of the Honda family.

242
00:15:43,660 --> 00:15:46,320
Are you still spouting such dreamy nonsense?

243
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:49,620
The Honda family will
always be a motorcycle shop.

244
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:53,780
This is an eco-friendly era
that's kind to the planet now.

245
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:57,340
Motorcycles spewing exhaust
fumes should just disappear.

246
00:15:58,620 --> 00:16:00,980
Let me show you the true
power of the bicycle!

247
00:16:00,980 --> 00:16:03,200
Don't underestimate me,
even if you're a demon.

248
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:15,760
Eeeeeeh!

249
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:20,080
Eeeeeeh!

250
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:20,580
Eeeeeeh!

251
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:28,260
Ugh, what a father-son fight this is!

252
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:30,400
Senpai, won't you stop them?

253
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:33,940
This is a world I just can't keep up with.

254
00:16:33,940 --> 00:16:35,880
When things like this happen, you see,

255
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:37,120
Here we go.

256
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,480
This is the best way.

257
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:46,480
Dad, Monkey, cut it out already!

258
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,580
Don't stop me, Hayato!

259
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:49,760
This has nothing to do with you,
big brother!

260
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:54,340
You idiot,
you embarrassed us in front of the customer!

261
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:56,020
Stay out of this.

262
00:16:56,020 --> 00:17:07,000
Your family is way too over the top.

263
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,900
They had a huge fight at
the shop yesterday too,

264
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:12,200
and apparently they've been cleaning
up the mess since this morning.

265
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,980
So that's why the shop was closed.

266
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:16,060
Are you alright, Dad?

267
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,580
Sorry about this, Eve.

268
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:24,000
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

269
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,700
I haven't even said anything yet, you know!

270
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:28,620
What's wrong with Senpai Eve?

271
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:32,980
Growing up surrounded by a family like this,
the kid must have a hard time of it.

272
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:36,280
If you've got any complaints,
you'd better say them straight out.

273
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:39,500
Men, if you leave them alone,
they go and start right up again.

274
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,460
Complaints? Nothing like that!

275
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:48,380
Whoa, it's the Rikuo Seven!

276
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:52,620
A used bike in this condition,
you'll never see another one like it.

277
00:17:52,620 --> 00:17:54,000
This one's brand new.

278
00:17:56,860 --> 00:17:58,680
Don't think I'm some Fukashigi Ren!

279
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:01,280
There's no way there's a new Rikuo!

280
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:05,640
I won't sell a bike to people
who can't even tell new from used!

281
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:06,720
Get out!

282
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:08,460
Hey, who said no!

283
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,160
I want this one!

284
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,320
I'm not moving until you sell it to me!

285
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:14,680
No, I've already reserved that bike!

286
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:16,520
I've taken the test, too, you know!

287
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:18,960
What? There's a test?

288
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:22,560
Yeah, though for punks like you,

289
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:25,000
you won't even pass the first test.

290
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:28,360
You don't know until you try!
Let me take it!

291
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:30,620
I doubt it'll do any good.

292
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:32,400
Guh...

293
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:35,020
That's why I said it was pointless.

294
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:39,660
This isn't a place for
half-baked punks like you to come!

295
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:41,020
Get lost, now!

296
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:42,480
I don't remember you!

297
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:45,640
Who'd remember you!
Don't you ever come back!

298
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:47,460
Hey Eve, let's get the salt out!

299
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:48,440
Right.

300
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:52,080
So what about my test...?

301
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:53,700
That's right. Well then,

302
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,420
where were we?

303
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:01,560
It's the ninth test!
We already did the written exam, didn't we!

304
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:04,320
But where's the answer sheet?

305
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:07,680
Found it.

306
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,180
It can't be helped.

307
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:17,680
I guess you'll have to take
it again from the beginning.

308
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,540
Do I have to do all of
that again from the start?

309
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:22,500
When we went touring,

310
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:25,840
we found an old motorcycle
abandoned at the bottom of a ravine.

311
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:27,160
What would you do?

312
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:29,420
I might actually die!

313
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:33,440
Dad, Sis...

314
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:34,420
No way.

315
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:38,600
Hib

316
00:19:39,220 --> 00:19:40,380
Dad, this...

317
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:47,040
We have your daughter.
If you want her back, bring the Rikuo.

318
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:49,060
The second sheet is a map.

319
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:51,920
Those bastards...

320
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:56,960
What should we do?
Maybe we should tell the police after all.

321
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:58,620
We are the police.

322
00:19:58,620 --> 00:19:59,740
That's right.

323
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:03,100
Aaaaaah!

324
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:12,560
Oh-san, that's not a Ricoh, it's a double-something!
I can't hand our bike over to a river current!

325
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:16,880
Eeeeeh! I'll make you publicly
admit you picked a fight with Honda!

326
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:22,940
Stop right there!

327
00:20:23,420 --> 00:20:23,894
Hey!

328
00:20:23,944 --> 00:20:52,800
Nah, nah, nah, nah, nah...

329
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:54,400
Monkey!

330
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:55,780
Bite him!

331
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:56,620
Move!

332
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,560
Patil!

333
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:02,960
He's already here!

334
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:03,600
Damn it!

335
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:06,660
I won't let him get away!

336
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:10,280
Damn!

337
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:12,220
Bicycles just don't have enough power.

338
00:21:12,220 --> 00:21:13,600
Leave it to me!

339
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:15,720
Big brother! I'm counting on you!

340
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:17,220
I'm going too!

341
00:21:18,260 --> 00:21:19,600
Dad, don't overdo it!

342
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:29,620
Minami-Senju is my turf.

343
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:32,540
If you think you can get away,
you're dead wrong.

344
00:21:41,540 --> 00:21:42,920
Uh-oh, this is bad.

345
00:21:55,780 --> 00:21:56,980
The elephant's escaped!

346
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:06,000
M!

347
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:07,800
What do we do?

348
00:22:12,420 --> 00:22:13,460
Where's Eve?

349
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:14,620
She's up there!

350
00:22:18,620 --> 00:22:19,640
She did it!

351
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:21,700
She managed to climb
onto the elephant's back.

352
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:23,880
Here,

353
00:22:24,900 --> 00:22:25,580
big sis...

354
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:26,800
she's safe now.

355
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:28,080
She's on top of that elephant.

356
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:29,000
Elephant

357
00:22:29,720 --> 00:22:30,600
Uh-oh.

358
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:31,680
What's wrong?

359
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:32,880
What's the problem?

360
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:34,860
I just remembered something.

361
00:22:34,860 --> 00:22:39,060
Even quiet Eve changed her personality once.

362
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:42,700
Before Eve started kindergarten,

363
00:22:42,700 --> 00:22:47,200
when she went to the circus
and got to ride an elephant,

364
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:50,860
Eve-chan changed as soon
as she got on the elephant.

365
00:22:57,720 --> 00:22:59,080
This is the worst-case scenario.

366
00:22:59,660 --> 00:23:02,100
Get off, we're going home.

367
00:23:02,100 --> 00:23:03,540
Get off?

368
00:23:04,940 --> 00:23:07,420
It's your fault for fighting, you two!

369
00:23:07,980 --> 00:23:10,020
That has nothing to do with this!

370
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:12,080
You dare defy me?

371
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:12,980
Hah!

372
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:14,020
Haaah!

373
00:23:15,180 --> 00:23:16,000
Whoa!

374
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:18,560
Haaah!

375
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,060
Haaah!

376
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:23,100
Haaah!

377
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:29,280
Stop it!

378
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:36,000
It's your fault for having a shop like this!

379
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:39,740
My artificial...!

380
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:43,380
Stop it, Eve!

381
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:46,440
Sis, please don't wreck my room!

382
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:48,040
Stop!

383
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:49,680
Move, move! Move, move!

384
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:51,680
Kiritebuu

385
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:55,700
At this rate, the father-son quarrel
is going to be put on hold for a while.

386
00:24:16,560 --> 00:24:23,700
shouting, with spirit,
resolved, quickly, helping

387
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:35,360
settled, inspired, bouncing,
wrapping up, acting, flying off

388
00:24:36,260 --> 00:24:40,040
Above all, amazing power

389
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:52,340
Everyone gather, come here,
the dreamlike final energy

390
00:24:53,360 --> 00:25:03,480
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, drawing the universe,
standing on the ground, the star of Kameari spun around in a circle.

391
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:08,700
"This'll do, right?" "Like hell it will!"

392
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:23,740
Thank you for watching.

393
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:43,720
Thank you for watching.

